{
  "title": "The Grimm Forest",
  "seed": 11,
  "comment": "Three pigs race to finish three houses. The gather half is why this game is here: everybody commits a Gather card face down, the pigs walk out together, and a Location divides what lies on it by the number of pigs standing there — a compute with a '/' in it, read once before anybody collects, so the second pig does not divide what the first left. The Gather card is where every 'at your Location' rule lives, because it is the only card in the round that knows where its owner went: it writes 'crowd' and 'mates' onto the seat, and a Fable then reads those rather than the board. What the file could not say is on the 'not_implemented' card.",
  "players": [
    { "card": "orange" },
    { "card": "blue" },
    { "card": "green" }
  ],

