    { "key": "not_implemented", "text": "What is missing", "tags": ["immutable"],
      "play": { "phases": [] },
      "tooltip": "The core game is whole: secret Gather cards, sharing a Location, the five build sites, the three sections in order, Friends on Walls, the First Builder Bonus and its three rewards, replenishment, the Starting Player passing, and the sturdiness tie-breakers.\n\nSix Fables and six Friends are in the decks. The rest of the box is not, and each one is out for a reason the format can name:\n\n- *Monsters and Unique Locations* — Wolf, Dragon, Giant, Big Bad Wolf, Bridge Troll, Grandma's House, Lonely Castle, Royal Wedding, Fairy Food. Each is played onto a Location the player names when it is revealed, and acts on that Location a step later. A card resolved by a phase carries no target, and a destination may not be named by a tag, so the card cannot be put where it was sent.\n\n- *Handing something to one named opponent* — the keep-or-give rule on every Friend, and Night at the Tavern, Sleeping Beauty, Thoughtful Gift, Snow White, Share the Wealth, A Friendly Game. A destination is a zone or a card, and there is no way to say \"that player's copy of this zone\".\n\n- *Peeking at, and swapping, face-down cards* — Crystal Ball, Wishing Well, Evil Queen, Curse of Darkness, Roar. Hidden information that holds against a determined opponent is not something this engine offers.\n\n- *Declaring out loud* — Aladdin, Pinocchio. There is no channel to say it on.\n\nAlso left out: the two-player game (Prince Regal and his die) and the four-player game (the Market). This is the three-player game." },

